			<div class="content" id="post-content-2400557">
									

<p>Alright apparently I'm going to have to read this twice, because the first time through I just can't find myself really caring about&#8230; any of it. Maybe I had missed something, I don't know.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Title&nbsp;for&nbsp;showing&nbsp;text</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Title&nbsp;for&nbsp;hiding&nbsp;text</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Why would there even /be/ links to differing versions of the thing in what is apparently an actual <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-2111/offset/0">database page</a>?</p>
<p>Why is the <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-2111/offset/1">RED TALISMAN</a> article not Thaumiel?</p>
<p>In <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-2111/offset/2">RIDDEN TONGUE</a> why would an antimeme thing create kill agents? Honestly due to the apparently mixed nature of what this does in terms of cognitohazards (which I assume are delivered via memes) and antimemes, I don't know why the Memetics Division would be led to believe RED TALISMAN is legit.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This file and all associated documents are for Counterconceptual Division eyes only.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The what?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Description: SCP-2111 is a hostile antimemetic entity</p>
</blockquote>
<p>And&#8230; the antimeme team isn't allowed to know about it. Why?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>antimemetic infovore</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I thought infovore was just a newbie's way of saying antimeme because they didn't know what an antimeme was.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This will trigger an institutional &quot;witch hunt&quot; within the Memetics Division</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You&#8230; Why would putting quotes around something magically make it immune to tone requirements?</p>
<p>Seriously what is the Counterconceptual Division? Why does it exist? What is its purpose?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>If you can read this, you are already dead.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Ghosts have access to the Foundation database.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Future manifestations of SCP-2111-like entities are to be identified and destroyed with targeted antimemetic agents.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Wait now we have antimeme agents?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>While no Ω-0 personnel are able to recall events between their deaths and 04/21/1981</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&#8230;Did&#8230; did they die <em>before</em> 1981? Are you saying the Foundation actually talks to ghosts?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Hypotheses include: the human noosphere, the astral plane and the quantum informational level of space-time.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>How is 'the astral plane' clinical?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>O5:8</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-2111 gradually built a following of deceased personnel, and taught them the techniques to create and deploy these attacks.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is seriously just casually stating there are ghosts. Which I am one of, because I am reading this document.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Okay yeah still not a fan. While the story present in REVENANT THEORY and READ THIS are kinda neat, they're really hampered down by the previous tabs, what I feel are a fair amount of tone issues, and&#8230; well, the Counterconceptual Division. I'm guessing they're supposed to be responsible for orchestrating lies within the Foundation? Or something? But I don't know why the Foundation is lying to itself here.</p>
<p>It feels like you're trying to do to many things at once here, some of which I found poorly explained, some of which just wasn't interesting, which in turn hampered anything I did think could have been cool.</p>
<p>quickedit: Oop, meant to say- I will give kudos for the little wikimagic of having the offsets all get one rating module and discussion page. That's actually really cool.</p>

							</div>

								
