			<div class="content" id="post-content-2400696">
									

<p>Wait, how did you make the comments pages the same on all of these? @_@</p>
<p>Okay, well, after getting to the end, I have to say, I am incredibly disappointed. Here's my train of thought:</p>
<p>Iteration 0: Oh boy here we go time for another one of <em>these</em> it looks stupid.</p>
<p>Iteration 1: Well, it's cute.</p>
<p>Iteration 2: Still just getting deeper into the rabbit hole, but at least it's written well. I suspect the next one will be Keter and the 'real' one Thaumiel.</p>
<p>Iteration 3: Holy shit this is awesome. Infovores and Foundation departments turning against themselves and each other? Sign me up! The next one's gonna be sweet! I can't wait to piece this together!</p>
<p>Which brings us to iteration 4. Now don't get me wrong, the story of Michelle Yu is really compelling and preventing me from downvoting. I love that collapsible, which I think is a pretty solid callback to that deleted article, and it <em>is</em> a story, which so often gets overlooked in articles. But I can't see the whole &quot;Welcome to Team Foundation Data Ghosts!&quot; thing as incredibly silly. It's an anime plot. It's just an incredible letdown after all that buildup, and I'm not sure I can adequately articulate why. :(</p>

